Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is “financial point of view” the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 9.3. Change of Recommendation. <omitted> (f) Notwithstanding anything in this Agreement to the contrary, the Company Board may effect a Company Adverse Recommendation Change <omitted> if, and only if, <omitted> (iii) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with the Company’s outside legal counsel and strategic advisors, that the failure to make the Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law, (iv) the Company has provided Parent written notice of the Company Board’s intention to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement not earlier than 11:59 p.m. New York time on the fifth Business Day after Parent receives such written notice and (v) the decision to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change is in connection with an Acquisition Proposal that meets regulatory compliance standards and the Company shall have complied with clauses (1) through (6), as follows: (1) prior to giving effect to clauses (2) through (6), the Company Board shall have determined that such Acquisition Proposal is a Superior Proposal, (2) the Company shall have made available to Parent the material terms and conditions of such Acquisition Proposal, (3) the Company shall have negotiated in good faith with Parent, to the extent that Parent desires to negotiate, during the five Business Day period with respect to such proposed revisions to this Agreement or other proposals made by Parent, if any, so that the Acquisition Proposal would no longer constitute a Superior Proposal, (4) after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and taking into account the proposals made by Parent, if any, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, strategic advisors, and a financial advisor of nationally recognized reputation, the Company Board shall have determined in good faith that such Acquisition Proposal remains a Superior Proposal, and, after consultation with its outside legal counsel and strategic advisors, that the failure to make the Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law and (5) if the Company intends to terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, the Company shall have complied with Section 10.1(d)(i). For clarity, the provisions of this Section 9.3(f) shall also apply to any amendment to the financial terms or any other material amendment to any Acquisition Proposal (except that any reference to five Business Days shall instead be three Business Days) or any successive Acquisition Proposals. (Pages 89-90)\nAnswer:
